<p class="tk-prose__lead">In force since 6 October 2026. Second edition: adds the gallery, messages and groups, comments, venue cameras and the watermark on photos and videos.</p>

<h3>1. Who we are and what this is</h3>
<p>Takebana is a platform for live streams, video calls, messaging and venues with cameras at takebana.com, operated by Murat Kunizhev, Republic of Serbia (“we”, “us”). For general questions write to <a href="mailto:contact@takebana.com">contact@takebana.com</a>. For data, rights and content complaints, write to <a href="mailto:private@takebana.com">private@takebana.com</a>.</p>
<p>These terms are an agreement between you and us. By opening the site, creating an account, going live or watching someone else’s stream, you accept them. If you do not accept them, you may not use the platform.</p>
<p>How we handle your data is described separately, in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and the <a href="/cookies">cookie notice</a>.</p>

<h3>2. Age</h3>
<p>The platform is for adults. You must be 18 or older to create an account, stream, call or send messages. If we learn that an account belongs to someone under 18, we delete it.</p>
<p>Authors can mark a stream as “18+”. Such a stream opens only after the viewer confirms their age, and that confirmation is the viewer’s own statement, not a document check.</p>

<h3>3. Your account</h3>
<ul>
<li>An account is created with an email and password, or through Google sign-in.</li>
<li>The details you give at sign-up must be true, and your password must stay known only to you. You are responsible for everything done from your account.</li>
<li>One person, one account. Accounts may not be transferred, sold or rented.</li>
<li>You can delete your account yourself: Settings → Delete account. Your streams, recordings, gallery photos and videos, comments, venues, messages with attachments, calls, contacts and subscriptions are deleted with it and cannot be restored.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4. What is and is not allowed</h3>
<p>You are responsible for everything you show, write and upload. The following is forbidden on the platform:</p>
<ul>
<li>any sexual material involving minors, and any attempt to groom children; we report such material to law enforcement;</li>
<li>violence, threats, and calls for violence or unlawful acts;</li>
<li>bullying, harassment, insults, and hatred based on race, nationality, religion, sex, orientation, disability and similar characteristics;</li>
<li>other people’s material you have no rights to: films, music, match broadcasts, other people’s videos and photographs;</li>
<li>other people’s personal data without their consent, and filming people who have not agreed to be filmed;</li>
<li>deception, fraud, pyramid schemes, and the sale of prohibited goods;</li>
<li>spam: mass identical messages, comments and group invitations;</li>
<li>interference with the platform: password guessing, automated scraping, bypassing limits, and attempts to reach other people’s accounts.</li>
</ul>
<p>Filming inside a venue is the venue owner’s responsibility: they must tell guests and staff about the camera and comply with local law on filming in public places.</p>

<h3>5. Streams, recordings and the gallery</h3>
<ul>
<li>You keep the rights to your videos and photos. We receive the right to show them on the platform: deliver them to viewers, store them, make a cover image, and display them in the catalogue, the feed, search and on your page.</li>
<li>A stream is recorded only if you choose “Save recording” when you finish. Recordings and gallery photos and videos are kept until you delete them or delete your account.</li>
<li>You can open a stream to your subscribers only. Who may comment on your posts is set in your privacy settings.</li>
<li><strong>We put a Takebana watermark on images and video.</strong> On a live stream and a venue camera it is shown over the picture; on recordings, cover images, gallery photos and videos, and photos and videos in messages it is part of the frame. Removing, covering or cropping it is not allowed.</li>
<li>We do not promise that a stream will run without interruptions, and we are not liable for a recording or file lost to a failure of equipment, connection or contractor services.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6. Messages and calls</h3>
<ul>
<li>Who may message you, call you and add you to groups is set in your privacy settings. You can also close your page and conversations to a particular person.</li>
<li>A disappearing message vanishes for the recipient after it is viewed or its time runs out, but we cannot stop the recipient from photographing the screen.</li>
<li>We do not record calls. A group’s owner and its admins manage its members and are responsible for order in it.</li>
</ul>

<h3>7. Venues</h3>
<p>A venue owner publishes a card with the name, address, phone, email, opening hours and a point on the map, and is responsible for those details being correct. Applications are reviewed by an administrator; we may refuse to publish a card or take it down without giving reasons. The venue camera is switched on by the owner, who is also responsible for what it shows; the picture goes out only while someone is watching and is not stored. The owner is also responsible for the video menu and the venue description. Visitors can rate venues.</p>

<h3>8. Complaints and copyright</h3>
<p>If material on the platform infringes your rights, write to <a href="mailto:private@takebana.com">private@takebana.com</a>. Give the link to the material, explain the infringement and show that the rights are yours. We review such letters and remove the material when the infringement is confirmed.</p>
<p>Streams, recordings, photos, videos, comments, messages and users can also be reported with the flag button. Reports are handled by moderation.</p>

<h3>9. Moderation</h3>
<p>We may stop a stream, delete a recording, a photo, a video, a comment, a message or a venue card, restrict an account or delete it if these terms or the law are broken. In urgent cases we act immediately and without warning. If you believe a decision is wrong, write to us.</p>

<h3>10. Disclaimer</h3>
<p>The platform is provided “as is”. We do not promise that it works without interruption or error, and we give no warranty that it fits your purposes.</p>
<p>Streams, recordings, the gallery, comments, messages and venue cards are created by users. We neither write them nor review them in advance, so we are not responsible for them. We do not verify venue details and are not a party to your dealings with a venue.</p>
<p>We are not liable for lost profit, lost data or indirect losses. Where the law allows liability to be limited, our total liability to you is limited to what you have paid us over the last twelve months, and to zero if you have paid nothing.</p>
<p>We are not liable for outages of the third-party services the platform relies on: video calling, storage, video delivery, email, browser notification services, and the server provider.</p>

<h3>11. Payment</h3>
<p>Use of the platform is currently free. If paid features appear, we will describe them separately and give notice in advance.</p>

<h3>12. Changes</h3>
<p>We may change these terms. A new edition takes effect on the date shown at the top of this page. If you keep using the platform after that date, you have accepted the changes.</p>

<h3>13. Law and disputes</h3>
<p>These terms are governed by the law of the Republic of Serbia. We try to settle disputes by correspondence first: write to us and we will reply. If that fails, the dispute goes to the court at the platform’s place of administration, unless the law of your country gives you the right to another court.</p>
